    {
      "context_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
      "version": 1,
      "statement": "Finite review of every mathematical unit represented by the 239 artifacts in PRIOR_DRAFTS.json. Source manuscripts at manifest revision 4eaee87548250b2682affda7d05d947c05554bae are references, not authority to change the objective. Engineer findings are opinions; native independent Reviewer acceptance remains required.",
      "definitions": {
        "B": "k[x,y,z,u]/(xy-z(z+1))",
        "C": "k[a,d,b,c,u]/(ac-bd-1)",
        "s": "y-x(x+u^2)",
        "I": "(x-s^2+u^2,z-s*x) in B",
        "fiber_weight": "(1,1,-1,-1,0) on (a,d,b,c,u)",
        "auxiliary_degree": "(0,1,-1,0,1) on (a,d,b,c,u)",
        "LND": "k-linear derivation for which each element is killed by some iterate; no uniform exponent assumed",
        "f": "x1-2*Q*(Q*(x2+x4)+x1*x4), Q=x2^2-x4^2+x1*x3",
        "September_S": "2*u^3*v+3*u^4*w+h*(v^2-3*u^2*w^2)+h^2*w^3",
        "September_F": "h-(-2*s^2*x+3*s*y^2-3*s^3*y)-1, with x=u^3+h*v, y=-u^2+h*w, s=September_S"
      },
      "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
    }
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "OCT_STABLE_PRESENTATION",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Over C, the exact signed determinant substitution identifies C[p,s,u,F,J]/(H) with C[x1,x2,x3,x4], carrying p to literal f; adjoining one independent variable makes p a coordinate, and every p=lambda quotient is C^[3]. Here x=s^2-u^2+p*F and H=x^2*F-(1+2*s*x)*J-p*J^2-u.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "4f1e0cae5e5dca2e569de151504dcaca3180d493e4c1a3fbac2afa667f4bc85a"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "OCT_UNRESTRICTED",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For every characteristic-zero field k, every nonzero locally nilpotent k-derivation E of the exact B, and every h in the exact I, E(h)=0 implies h=0.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "eb8dd97ba3e5e93902f5fe5b8a92de185ce898a0be4ccfb7fff92315aa52061a"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "OCT_COORDINATE_TRANSFER",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Over C, if the distinguished p is a polynomial coordinate of A=C[p,s,u,F,J]/(H), there exist a nonzero LND E of B and a nonzero h in I with E(h)=0. The source filtration is integer indexed, exhaustive and separated, and the argument allows negative leading shifts.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "b41d9a46e70bf8c5d57fe0a7ce5ca55215e7b659380e7ba6ee7212faf36b1bdf"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "OCT_ACTION_LIFT",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For a characteristic-zero field k, B injects into C by (x,y,z,u)=(ab,dc,db,u), and every LND E of B has a locally nilpotent lift D to C extending E and preserving each actual fiber-weight space. Nonzero E gives nonzero D.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "1053434a255aa3fe94983ea44a81fe8208144cb427f293622d8a94fb545bfb3c"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "OCT_COMPOSITE",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For the complex exact B and I, every nonzero LND has zero invariant intersection with I; coordinate literal f would produce a nonzero such invariant; consequently literal f is not a coordinate but is a one-stable coordinate. This is the unchanged natural statement of old C_STABLE_CORE_VERIFY versions 1,2,3.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "aff3cafa38cf656a75f6a3a8b3524dc25fe8dc342dd9eabc8bc42e289b216eac"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "OCT_LITERAL_PACKAGE",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
      },
      "natural_statement": "The exact complex literal f has total degree five, is not a coordinate in four variables, is one-stable, and every fibre is affine three-space with a nonrectifiable embedding in affine four-space.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "5abe5313f1b2512f2c6f6a588470bf82f4d5e860e9d2b663f38175c44f622811"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "SEP_LIFTING",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Over any commutative unital ring B, including zero divisors and the zero ring, x^2+y^3=h*s and (h,y)=B imply B[U,V,W]/(U^3+h*V-x,-U^2+h*W-y,September_S(h,U,V,W)-s) is B[T], by explicit polynomial inverses.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "4d7e6fddc0cea78234d1dbe9aaaefa25f9173e0d26cc53b4e11df52de0867d57"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "SEP_ZERO_CRITICAL",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For the literal September F defined in this context, C[h,u,v,w]/(F) is C^[3]; at (2,0,-1/2,1/2), F=-1 and all four partial derivatives vanish. Thus F is not a coordinate after adjoining any finite number of polynomial variables.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "8f90f2300866e29d047d7079db656ff33b7e7871fd15e6b3f4a8dadc2c60a5b7"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "GLOBAL_PRINCIPALIZATION",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For every commutative unital ring R and arbitrary a,d,b,c,t with ac-bd=1, set s=dc-ab*t and v=a^2*t-d^2. The ordinary ideals (t-s^2,bd-s*ab) and (v) are equal by integral polynomial witnesses, including in the zero ring.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "c36d4e8d03bd3c44d8a9268573600aac8fc58fe102296aa6b10a9c5bb67fc606"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "LOWER_PERTURBATION_RIGIDITY",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For every characteristic-zero field k, in the exact C with the context gradings, every fiber-weight-preserving LND D satisfying D(W+a^2*u^2-d^2)=0 is zero whenever W has no actual auxiliary homogeneous component in any degree above 1. No homogeneity of W is required.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "53169ec73fcee407c207e3b9a8a9ad1ccbbb7012013fe4f70701b526fd5e716a"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "UNIFORM_SURFACE_FAMILY",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_OLD_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "85537901b846d86b126112b26d8086c17f96d5cb4b7399167ec446a5267ece41"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Over C, for every psi in C[T] including zero and repeated-root polynomials, tpsi=u^2+psi(x), spsi=y-x*tpsi, Jpsi=(tpsi-spsi^2,z-spsi*x) satisfy Jpsi intersect ker(E)=0 for every nonzero LND E of B; B/Jpsi is C[X,R,V]/(R*V-psi(X)); no nonzero LND preserves the whole ideal Jpsi.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "49a4e3daab81624b7ad1d00b9242722bf2de6abc647c5108b26fe8c06417c4c3"
    },
